etain the original time unit: a half-life in years produces a rate per source year, without silently assuming a calendar conversion. Inequalities reverse for the reciprocal decay constant. Estimates remain estimates. Stable or unavailable half-lives have no numeric result. Symmetric uncertainty is propagated to first order; asymmetric source uncertainties remain unpropagated and visible. These calculations add no new experimental evidence or significant figures.\n\n<!-- ame2020-companion -->\n\n[Atomic masses, Q-values and separation energies](0083-Bismuth-Bi-Mass-and-Reaction-Evaluation.md) are available in the separate AME2020 companion, with ground-state, estimate and uncertainty semantics.\n",
